      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the smallest number divisible by integers 1 through 9, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of these numbers. The LCM of a set of integers is the smallest positive integer that is divisible by each of the integers in the set.\n\nWe can use the prime factorization method to find the LCM. First, we find the prime factorization of each integer from 1 to 9:\n\n1: 1\n2: 2\n3: 3\n4: 2^2\n5: 5\n6: 2 * 3\n7: 7\n8: 2^3\n9: 3^2\n\nNow, we take the highest power of each prime factor that appears in the factorizations:\n\n2^3 (from 8)\n3^2 (from 9)\n5 (from 5)\n7 (from 7)\n\nThe LCM is the product of these highest powers:\n\nLCM = 2^3 * 3^2 * 5 * 7\n\nLCM = 8 * 9 * 5 * 7\n\nLCM = 72 * 5 * 7\n\nLCM = 360 * 7\n\nLCM = 2520\n\nSo, the smallest number divisible by integers 1 through 9 is 2520.",
