    "text": "To find the smallest number divisible by integers 1 through 9, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of these numbers. The LCM of a set of integers is the smallest positive integer that is divisible by each of the integers in the set.\n\nWe can use the prime factorization method to find the LCM. First, we find the prime factorization of each number from 1 to 9:\n\n1: 1\n2: 2\n3: 3\n4: 2^2\n5: 5\n6: 2 * 3\n7: 7\n8: 2^3\n9: 3^2\n\nNow, we take the highest power of each prime factor that appears in the factorization of any of the numbers:\n\n2^3 (from 8)\n3^2 (from 9)\n5 (from 5)\n7 (from 7)\n\nFinally, we multiply these highest powers together to get the LCM:\n\nLCM = 2^3 * 3^2 * 5 * 7 = 8 * 9 * 5 * 7 = 2520\n\nSo, the smallest number divisible by integers 1 through 9 is 2520.",
